WHATNOW

What tam-data is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-19, with W2


STATE

  tam-data is a C11 rewrite of VisiData on libtam, for any terminal
  including the Linux console. Branch dev, pushed. VERSION reads 1.0.1.

  Phases 0 to 6 are complete (1.0.0, 2026-11-13): CSV, TSV, JSON, JSONL,
  INI, fixed-width and process-table loaders; navigation, selection,
  search, sorting, editing, undo, the command log and replay;
  aggregators, frequency tables, describe, pivot, melt and joins; the
  expression engine and computed columns; metasheets, the command
  palette, help and terminal plots.

  1.0.1, the performance patch, is in progress (ROADMAP.md): the
  benchmark harness is done (make bench, docs/BENCHMARKS.md, with the
  1.0.0 baselines); the rest is not started.

  Follows the tam-idol 0.1.0 standard (W2, 2026-11-19). That change
  touched READMEs, plans and records only; no code changed, so VERSION
  stays 1.0.1.


NEXT

  1. The rest of 1.0.1 (ROADMAP.md, "v1.0.1"), each with a target from
     the recorded baselines:
     - streaming JSONL loader in src/json.c: mmap and line-by-line
       parsing into a reusable scratch arena; 1M.jsonl from 1037.6 MiB
       and 2.07 s to at most 300 MiB and 500 ms;
     - single-pass describe_sheet in src/agg.c: 1M rows by 6 columns
       from 4.46 s to under 1 s;
     - CSV row pre-sizing and madvise(MADV_SEQUENTIAL) in src/csv.c and
       src/sheet.c;
     - then re-run make bench, update docs/BENCHMARKS.md with before
       and after, and check make test (ASan, UBSan) and make smoke.

  2. 1.1.0 (ROADMAP.md): cached string sort keys, a smaller td_val_t,
     cold-start tuning.

  3. Small fix: README still builds libtam into ~/.local/dev, which
     Tamlinux retired on 2026-11-17. Development installs now go to
     ~/.local (PREFIX=$HOME/.local), as libtam's README says. Update the
     build notes and the libtam discovery fixed in c907254.


